{
  "id": "ps_bgn_pcgn",
  "title": "Pashto — BGN/PCGN 1968 (2017 revision)",
  "language": "ps",
  "script": "Arab",
  "kind": "geographic",
  "status": "current",
  "year": 1968,
  "authority": "US Board on Geographic Names / UK Permanent Committee on Geographical Names, 1968 system, 2017 revision (results identical to the BGN/PCGN national system for Afghanistan, 2007)",
  "description": "BGN/PCGN romanization of Pashto geographical names (no UN system exists): retroflex ṯ ḏ ṟ ṉ, ts dz for څ ځ, z͟h s͟h for ږ ښ, w for و, vowels ē (ې), ō/ū (و), ê (zwarakay), êy (ۍ, ئ), final ی = ay, Arabic letters as in BGN/PCGN Persian; final h = -ah, ezafe -e/-ye, د = dê.",
  "sources": [
    "https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5ab4e57ee5274a1aa5933455/ROMANIZATION_OF_PASHTO.pdf",
    "https://www.eki.ee/wgrs/rom2_ps.pdf",
    "https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/romanisation-systems"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Pashto orthography distinguishes final ی (ay, masculine: Pōṯakay), ي (ī: Ghaznī), ې (ē), ۍ (êy) and ئ (êy); ى is folded onto ی.",
    "Note 7: the Arabic article is al at the start of a name and ul elsewhere, assimilated before sun letters, lower case and separate (Jabal us Sarāj). Note 5: -ābād, -zādah, -zay and -ullāh are joined to the preceding word (Raḩmatābād, Raḩmatullāh); -khwā and -shahr are not joined automatically.",
    "Note 2 (t͡s, d͡z with a tie bar) and Note 8 (shadda often omitted in Pashto spellings) are left to the input.",
    "The diphthong َی is written ay; the table also shows aī (Maīdān Shahr, Faīẕābād) next to ay (Maywand, Qayşār) without a rule, so aī is not generated.",
    "Unvocalised medial ی/ي after a consonant is ī and unvocalised و is ō (Khōst, Spīn Bōldak)."
  ],
  "alphabet": "ءآأؤئابپتټثجچځڅحخدډذرړزژږسشښصضطظعغفقکګگلمنڼوهیيېۍ",
